it feels so good to be making a Dark  Souls 3 video with actual footage so  about a month ago I put out a video  talking in depth about everything I had  learned from playing the gamescom demo  of Dark Souls 3 I talked about how the  game felt the bosses the enemies the  webinars and now we finally have footage  of that demo 4 minutes of it in fact  plus new info on magic covenants  multiplayer new game+ and more so let's  dive into it so if this is your first  time seeing Dark Souls 3 gameplay the  first thing you'll probably notice is  that a lot of these animations look  really similar to those in Dark Souls 1  and they are really similar in a  sentence what I've been saying lately is  that it feels like the mechanics and the  pacing of Dark Souls 1 but with the  polish and the fluidity of blood-borne  and Miyazaki confirms as much in an  interview he says that blood-borne  influenced a lot of the tuning and  adjustments to Dark Souls 3  however blood-borne doesn't have that  same role-playing element and the  customization of souls so he says that  the team will be focusing on those  things for Dark Souls 3 but let's talk a  little bit about the new features in  this demo it bears mentioning that this  demo that you're seeing here is an  updated version from one month ago there  are some new features we can talk about  like the mana bar magic and a cleric  style character who's featured towards  the end Dark Souls 3 still has a lot of  development to go before its release  date in April so bear that in mind but  by now you've probably noticed that  there's a mana bar in the top left  just like in Demon Souls in previous  demos this mana bar was a point system  and these points were consumed whenever  you used a weapon art ability now it's a  mana bar and both magic and weapon art  attacks will consume it if you don't  know what weapon arts are let me quickly  explain a weapon art is activated when  you press l2 and it opens up a couple of  new moves for your use depending on the  weapon that you're using so the short  swords weapon art is a stance 12 and art  you hold l2 and your character goes into  this stance from here you can press r1  to do a special uppercut  break attack or you can press r2 to do a  charging stab attack the greatswords  weapon art is a combo weapon art you  press l2 and your character slams the  sword down vertically but from there you  can press r2 to do a huge uppercut that  launches the enemy into the air  there are also some webinars that simply  activate when you press l2 for example  the scimitar does a spin attack and the  battle ax does a battle cry and there's  also the webinar for this mace that's  shown towards the end of this clip  though we can't tell what's happening  here from this short clip it's possible  that this webinar made his next attack  do more damage but it's also possible  that he didn't combo it properly I might  be able to try this out next time I get  my hands on the game if you have a  weapon art shield  designated by this little sword symbol  here you can use a weapon art with l2  with the shield still equipped if you  have a parry shield which is designated  by this symbol  you simply parry when you press l2 and  if you to hand your weapon you can use a  weapon art regardless of what she'll do  you have equipped so that mana bar in  the top left isn't just for casting  spells it's used for melee combat as  well mana doesn't appear to replenish  overtime but you can replenish it with a  new type of Estus flask which I believe  is called an ash Estus flask it's  visible in the bottom left the little  blue flask there so now when you're  going through a level you have to  sparingly use your Estus flask for  health and your ash Estus flask for mana  so it's another layer on top of a system  that was already a good system to begin  with so I can't imagine this being a bad  thing but let's move on to actual spells  as far as I know we know of six spells  so far there's soul arrow soul great  sword and soul dart which you can see  here for miracles there's lightning  spear a healing spell and sacred oath  which increases your attack and defense  for a short while obviously there'll be  more spells in fact in an interview with  game informer Miyazaki has stated that  players will have more criteria to  accurately choose the types of spells  that will fit your tactics or your  strategies and while the spells that  we've seen here are pretty standard bear  in mind we haven't heard  about what a weapon art for magic does  so I assume it's some way of deepening  the magic system let's move on to some  of the information revealed by a Game  Informer first up is covenants Miyazaki  mentions that he wants covenants to be  easier to understand on this topic he  says that covenants have always had  separate rules depending on each of the  covenants but this time we're thinking  of maintaining a common rule across the  covenants regarding invasions and  summoning so for example I take this  quote to mean that there could be one  covenant item for everybody regardless  of your covenant but the covenant you're  in determines what this item does like  an invasion item that changes the type  of enemy you invade based on your  covenant next is something that I'm  really excited about for me one of the  best things about a Souls game is that  thrill of being invaded and of invading  somebody else and it looks like these  systems are going to be simplified which  means that these systems are going to  become more popular Miyazaki states that  invasions and summoning will no longer  be locked behind consumable items which  naturally will help invasions become  more plentiful he also states that soul  memory is being removed which is good  and they're also aiming for six-person  multiplayer functionality let's quickly  talk about fast travel players will now  be able to fast travel from the very  beginning of the game since Miyazaki  apparently liked the convenience that  brought to Dark Souls 2  there has been no information on the  room and mechanic where you can create  your own bonfire via sacrifice so we'll  have to wait and see if that changes the  pacing of the game if it does end up  existing but moving on remember the soul  vessel from Dark Souls 2 it was an item  that allowed you to Reese Peschel eyes  your character and put your soul level  points in different categories  apparently it's returning for Dark Souls  3 in some form next is New Game+ one of  the best things about Dark Souls 2 was  new game+ and the fact that it offered  new enemies and new enemy placements and  new experiences game informer reveals  that this system will be returning  however bonfire ascetics that allow you  to  and an area to New Game+ to farm certain  enemies and face certain bosses again  will not be returning and next is  durability miyazaki mentions that he's  still tuning the balance on durability  and he wants weapons to break more  slowly than in Dark Souls 2 but faster  than in Dark Souls 1 so summer in the  middle and finally hidden walls are  returning and unlike in Dark Souls 2 you  have to actually hit the hidden wall to  unveil it and before you go I want to  let you know one more thing I'm going to  be playing the TGS demo tomorrow or  maybe today by the time this video is  released and I'm definitely going to  learn more about the demo so I'll be  putting this new information in the top  line of the description and also on  Twitter so if you're watching this on  the day it came out then follow me on  Twitter so you don't have to miss  anything but if you're not following  it's probably just in the first line of  the description I don't anticipate that  I'll be able to learn too much more from  playing the updated demo but I'll  definitely learn more about weapons and  a couple of new spells so that'll be  cool  but thanks for watching guys I got to  say I'm really excited for Dark Souls 3  just because it'll bring the community  back together which is a nice thing and  it's sounding pretty good so far so let  me know what you think in the comments I  still read them all so don't leave that  box empty and yeah I'll see you guys in  the next one
 

